{"title":"Career roadmap — Furniture Designer","role":"Furniture Designer","summary":"A Furniture Designer creates functional, ergonomic and aesthetically compelling furniture for homes, offices, hospitality, healthcare, retail and public spaces. The role combines industrial design, interior design, materials, manufacturing, ergonomics and user research.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)","Course":"Interior Design"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build design, materials, CAD, ergonomics and prototyping fundamentals"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Specialise in furniture categories, materials, manufacturing or sustainable design"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Lead product collections, furniture brands or design teams"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Become a design director, furniture entrepreneur, studio founder or strategic design leader"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Design fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design principles"},{"text":"Drawing and sketching"},{"text":"Perspective"},{"text":"Form and proportion"},{"text":"Colour theory"},{"text":"Design history"},{"text":"Basic model making"},{"text":"Introduction to materials"},{"text":"Human-centred design"},{"text":"Furniture history"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop strong hand-sketching and visualisation skills."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Furniture design fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ergonomics"},{"text":"Anthropometrics"},{"text":"Furniture construction"},{"text":"Wood and wood composites"},{"text":"Metal"},{"text":"Glass"},{"text":"Plastics"},{"text":"Upholstery"},{"text":"Joinery"},{"text":"Structural fundamentals"},{"text":"Material selection"},{"text":"Sustaina